**1. ArmOperation.cs** - IL2087/IL2090: `IsResource<T>()` uses reflection on `typeof(T)` (GetConstructor and Activator.CreateInstance). Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers]` to the type parameter T. The method needs `NonPublicConstructors` for both calls.

Current code (lines 96-111):
```csharp
private static bool IsResource<T>() where T : notnull
{
    var isResource = typeof(T).GetConstructor(
                    BindingFlags.NonPublic | BindingFlags.Instance,
                    null,
                    CallingConventions.Any,
                    new Type[] { typeof(ArmClient), typeof(ResourceIdentifier) },
                    null) is not null;
    var obj = Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), BindingFlags.NonPublic | BindingFlags.Instance, null, null, null);
    if (!isResource && obj is not IJsonModel<object>)
    {
        throw new InvalidOperationException($"Type {typeof(T)} should be Resource or Model");
    }

    return isResource;
}
```

Fix: Change to `private static bool IsResource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>() where T : notnull`

Make sure `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` is present in the usings.

**2. GenericOperationSource.cs** - IL2087: `CreateResult` uses `ModelReaderWriter.Read(data, typeof(T))` which needs `PublicConstructors | NonPublicConstructors`, and `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), ...)` which needs `NonPublicConstructors`.

Current class declaration (line 16):
